 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Try moving the chair back from the wall, so you' not right up against it. You could also try using a thick blanket on the back of the chair. Then move the chair out from the wall and start there. A thick blanket can make a big difference. Then try using a pop filter on the microphone. It's like a big piece of cloth that you wrap around the microphone. It reduces the echo. Stick it as close as possible without touching the back of the chair. If you can get it five inches away, it'll make a big difference. Good idea. Start out far away from the wall and move in while you record bit. That way you can hear the difference.",
